          "segment_id": "seg-86a41cf2aad6117f2467c3ed",
          "segment_index": 11,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-86a41cf2aad6117f2467c3ed",
          "source_text_sha256": "8f45f3d61e8f41d7f8987fa4d3e3ad5739919f010ce4cab6f7dc15370a8f15eb",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On July 27, 2015 at 8:00 pm (Tahiti time) a witness observed a long, glowing trail with parts detaching and moving East-West. The continuous observation lasted between 30 and 40 seconds. The phenomenon disappeared behind clouds. Only one testimony was collected. Given the collected elements, namely: - The reentry time is identical to that of the observation. - Existing records on the SATOBS site. - The physical and dynamic characteristics of the observation are in every way similar to those of a reentry of space debris. The GEIPAN classifies this case as 'A' as a certain observation of the disintegration upon entry into the atmosphere of a Soyuz rocket stage cataloged under the number \"15035B/40745\", the day after its resupply of the ISS.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "e9eeadb19937cce007515460f087401bc08a2408328a8b09a5b969e318dc9370"
        }
